WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.941
In this video, you will see how many people found your contest: page visits, visits from your QR code, and votes, day by day.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.574
That tells you which kind of sharing works.

00:00:10.574 --> 00:00:11.771
We start on the map.

00:00:12.671 --> 00:00:14.420
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:16.055 --> 00:00:18.572
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:20.318 --> 00:00:21.299
Then tap Allow.

00:00:25.089 --> 00:00:27.778
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:28.973
See the three dots?

00:00:28.973 --> 00:00:33.276
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:33.276 --> 00:00:33.814
Tap them.

00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:37.228
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:38.903 --> 00:00:44.001
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:00:44.702 --> 00:00:45.619
Tap Mine.

00:00:47.507 --> 00:00:49.084
This is your personal page.

00:00:49.084 --> 00:00:54.269
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:57.041
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:02.270
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:02.971 --> 00:01:05.255
Want to know whether your sharing is working?

00:01:05.255 --> 00:01:05.851
Tap Promote.

00:01:08.114 --> 00:01:17.052
Activity shows three numbers: how many people have visited your contest page, how many arrived by scanning your QR code, and how many people have voted.

00:01:17.952 --> 00:01:20.664
Below, a chart shows the votes for each day.

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:23.135
Use it to see which sharing worked best.

00:01:23.135 --> 00:01:27.957
If votes jump the day after a flyer went up, or after an email, do more of that.

00:01:28.858 --> 00:01:31.183
Next up: Add sponsors and logos.
